Z||000001||Nashco||11-02-2001||01:16 AM||||Most definitely!!!  This year was my first time, as I started going to school in Michigan last year.  I can't wait to go again, fully prepped with a good digital camera and a little more knowledge about the show in general.  I went to the Auto Show and the Autorama.  If you've never been to the Auto Show, I highly recommend it.  There are tons of sweet cars, and this is a very VERY good opportunity to brainstorm.  Seeing some of the designs that will never be or may someday be is fun, but thinking of how you could have that is even more fun.  This is also a great place to see exotic cars if you don't get to do that.  Heck, even if you like a good show, they put those on too.  I will surely follow the show a little more closely this year.<P>For those of you that live in Michigan, the Autorama is cool too.  This year Chris Moore's beautiful Northstar powered GT and a completely custom front-engine big block powered fiero...talk about HUGE tires, the whole rear of the car was tire!  I'm hoping Chris will enter again, and I can meet him and talk with him about his car.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||11-02-2001||01:33 AM||||Most Definitely!<P>Brent||||reg||14
